\label{thm-convergence}
    Let $F$ be a strictly 1-balanced graph with $s>0$ edges on $r \geq 2$ vertices. Given $c>0$, let $p= cn^{-1/\rd_1(F)}$ and $q=p^s=c^sn^{1-r}$.   There exists a constant $m(F,c)$ such that
    \begin{align*}
        \frac{{\rm MinM}(\mathbb{G}(n,p),F)}{n}
        \to m(F,c),
    \end{align*}
\whp~ as $n\to\infty$.

