\label{thm:main}
Let $c \neq 0$. 
Suppose ${\omega d}/{c}=1+\varepsilon$ for a sufficiently small absolute constant $\varepsilon > 0$ and ${\sigma}/{(c^{2}d)}>\frac13$, the system (\ref{main second}) admits a $C^2$ solitary wave solution with velocity $c$. Moreover, the solitary wave profile $\eta$ has the asymptotic expansion
\begin{equation}
\eta(\xi)=d\, \varepsilon\, Q\bigg(\varepsilon^{\frac{1}{2}}\bigg(\frac{\sigma}{c^2d}-\frac13\bigg)^{-\frac{1}{2}}\frac{\xi}{d}\bigg)+O(\varepsilon^2)
\end{equation}
where $Q(\bar x)=-3\mathrm{sech}^2(\bar x/2)$ solves the steady the KdV equation
\begin{equation}
Q''=Q+\frac{1}{2}Q^2.
\end{equation}

